{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/Kind-swift.struct","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/Kind-swift.struct\/Content-swift.enum"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Case","title":"MXLDirection.Kind.Content.metronome(_:)","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLDirectionV4KindV7ContentO9metronomeyAgA12MXLMetronomeVcAGmF","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"case","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"metronome","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLMetronome","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLMetronomeV"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"A metronome mark or other metric relationship.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/Kind-swift.struct\/Content-swift.enum\/metronome(_:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/kind-swift.struct\/content-swift.enum\/metronome(_:)"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"metronome","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLMetronome","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLMetronomeV"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/Kind-swift.struct/Content-swift.enum":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLDirection.Kind.Content","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/Kind-swift.struct\/Content-swift.enum","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One of the alternatives for DirectionType."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Content","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Content","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/kind-swift.struct\/content-swift.enum"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"displayed in the music notation."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLMetronome","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/Kind-swift.struct":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLDirection.Kind","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/Kind-swift.struct","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Textual direction types may have more than 1 component due to multiple fonts. The dynamics element may also be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used in the notations element. Attribute groups related to print suggestions apply to the individual"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"direction-type, not to the overall direction."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/kind-swift.struct"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/Kind-swift.struct/Content-swift.enum/metronome(_:)":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A metronome mark or other metric relationship."}],"title":"MXLDirection.Kind.Content.metronome(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/Kind-swift.struct\/Content-swift.enum\/metronome(_:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/kind-swift.struct\/content-swift.enum\/metronome(_:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"metronome"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLMetronomeV","text":"MXLMetronome"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLDirection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A direction is a musical indication that is not necessarily attached to a specific note. Two or more may be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"combined to indicate words followed by the start of a dashed line, the end of a wedge followed by dynamics,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"etc. For applications where a specific direction is indeed attached to a specific note, the direction element"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be associated with the first note element that follows it in score order that is not in a different voice."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDirection"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDirection"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection"}}}